    "question": {
        "text": "§\n\nWhen can Rifampin be used as a monotherapy?",
        "imageIds": []
    },
    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nWhen can Rifampin be used as a monotherapy?\n\nPROPHYLAXIS for those exposed to:\n\n(1) Neisseria meningitis\n\n(2) Haemophilus influenzae\n\n(Otherwise organisms quickly develop resistance)\n\n[Image: 1a8deaa81ef0ee0ee12c5b37f1859781041b580a49f8289cf7d8eb36e2adda19]\n\n[Image: c376c20e1387be735ad0adc48d87e9d55c2458d3631cf6afb5855a41fda1be7d]\n\n[Image: 0eefc86295686fb316799e73fea107f5695ab9f55218e25f1e8d559e97183df0]\n\n3.1 - Tuberculosis Drugs\n[Image: 75747c8b652c8f2d208a149207fab1b8976d4381798f86e53cbafe58b3751752]\n\n[Image: d4d07c3fd6d7ac606792eb4ace534fe4cdb21726d114d25beab0fdf8ec968a95]\n\n[Image: 8a6a87653f9aeb4a4876920b2a1558f23095df8b805d5c12e7f0a2e3f461200b]\n\n[Image: 263eda575dffc9aa3fccc786bb7febb77ffe5631bea7e464d00e08898ed80463]\n\n[Image: d564a2c26b1ad2fd2193e2653e6827fe68d6c771d1ae83265a06893ce8e50900]",
